From 8ca8affd98258327f4c3f81e05ed42a56e41f197 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t.io>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 14:27:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] refactor: cut fourteen sections to eight, remove unverifiable
 claims and dead links

Removed, with reasons:

- 'Proven impact in simulation and deployment' (22% curtailment reduction,
  sub-8 ms latency, 99.999% uptime, 15-40% renewable penetration). These are
  attributed to DERIM and NeuralBridge, neither of which is released. Nothing
  substantiates them.
- 'Standards Mastery' (IEC 61850, TLA+, NERC CIP, NIS2, EU CRA). 'Mastery' of
  eleven standards is not a claim a technical buyer will read charitably. The
  capability register already lists the protocols actually used, with provenance.
- 'Trusted Ecosystem' (MIT, IEA, NREL, BloombergNEF, AWS). Linking to
  institutions one has no relationship with borrows authority rather than
  demonstrating it.
- 'Live Intelligence Hub'. Two TradingView widgets (NVDA, MSFT, TSLA tickers),
  an rss2json news feed, and a GitHub repo fetch. A stock ticker on a personal
  engineering portfolio answers no question a visitor has, and the repo fetch
  returned nothing because every repository is private.
- 'Operational Time Zones' marquee. Five clocks and a 1 Hz interval.
- 'Architecture of Value Creation' and 'Flagship Systems'. Both restated what
  the capability register and work registry now say once, with provenance.
- The four 'strengths' cards under About. Same content, said twice.

Merged: About now carries the Deutsche Bahn experience directly beneath it,
so the claim and the job backing it are read together.

Every repository is private. Verified with git ls-remote against all six.
The site no longer renders 'View repository', 'View Source' or 'Star on
GitHub' links that 404 for visitors; private systems say so and route to
contact. When a repo is made public, restore its 'repo' URL in
app/lib/registry.ts and every surface starts linking to it again.

Header: four nav items instead of seven, and the 'Live SimulatorLIVE'
run-together label is gone.

Dead CSS: 56 rules removed, all with zero references in any .tsx.

Page size 22 kB -> 16.1 kB. First Load JS 110 kB -> 104 kB, below the
108 kB the site shipped before any of this work, despite adding the
palette, mega menu and registry.
